UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And he said, Yahuah (LORD) came from Sinai, and rose up from Seir unto them; he shined forth from mount Paran, and he came with ten thousands of saints: from his right hand went a fiery law for them.* (Deuteronomy 33:2). Moses sang of Yahuah (LORD) coming *with ten thousands of saints,* his fiery law going out from his right hand — the Sinai theophany that sets the pattern Paul invokes: the coming of our Lord *with all his saints* (1 Thessalonians 3:13). The same Yahuah (LORD) who came to Sinai for a people comes at the end for that people; the law that went forth at the first and the holiness in which the hearts are stablished at the last are one covenant, not two. *With all his saints* is not a host descending from heaven with him but the seed of promise raised up to him, as he was raised: *even so them also which sleep in Yahusha (Jesus) will Elohim (God) bring with him* (1 Thessalonians 4:14).'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=3 AND sv.verse_number=13
   AND tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='deuteronomy' AND tv.chapter_number=33 AND tv.verse_number=2
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His set-apart ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). The Hebrew library carried this same coming-with-the-saints word long before Thessalonica: *He cometh with ten thousands of His set-apart ones.* It is the very prophecy Paul leans on praying for hearts *unblameable in holiness... at the coming of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) with all his saints* (1 Thessalonians 3:13) — and the very prophecy Jude quotes by name as Enoch''s. The day he comes with all his saints is the day of judgement on the ungodly: the ungodly are convicted and burned first, and his set-apart ones, the seed of promise, are raised up and gathered to him. Zechariah and Moses sang the same coming, held in one voice across the whole library.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=3 AND sv.verse_number=13
   AND tv.edition_slug='enoch' AND tv.book_slug='1-enoch' AND tv.chapter_number=1 AND tv.verse_number=9
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And Enoch also, the seventh from Adam, prophesied of these, saying, Behold, Yahuah (Lord) cometh with ten thousands of his saints,* (Jude 14). Jude names the source: the coming-with-the-saints word is Enoch''s prophecy, *Behold, Yahuah (Lord) cometh with ten thousands of his saints.* This is the same coming Paul sets before the Thessalonians — *the coming of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) with all his saints* (1 Thessalonians 3:13). The saints Zechariah, Moses'' song, and Enoch''s prophecy name are the saints Paul names, the seed of promise; the day of his coming is witnessed by the whole library, when the Formed returns to judge the ungodly and to raise and gather his saints to himself.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=3 AND sv.verse_number=13
   AND tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='jude' AND tv.chapter_number=1 AND tv.verse_number=14
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And it shall come to pass in that day, that the great trumpet shall be blown, and they shall come which were ready to perish in the land of Assyria, and the outcasts in the land of Egypt, and shall worship Yahuah (LORD) in the holy mount at Jerusalem.* (Isaiah 27:13). The trump of the gathering is Isaiah''s: *the great trumpet shall be blown,* and the scattered outcasts of Yashar''el (Israel) *shall come* to worship Yahuah (LORD). This is the trumpet behind *Yahuah (Lord) himself shall descend from heaven with a shout... and with the trump of Elohim (God): and the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first* (1 Thessalonians 4:16). The great trumpet sounds at his coming: the trump of Elohim (God) raises the dead in Messiah (Christ), the righteous seed, and the regathering of the scattered outcasts that Isaiah foretold follows his return — not a secret summons severed from Yashar''el (Israel), but the day Yahuah (LORD) calls his own home.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=4 AND sv.verse_number=16
   AND tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='isaiah' AND tv.chapter_number=27 AND tv.verse_number=13
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* (Daniel 12:2). Daniel saw the resurrection: *many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake.* Paul writes of *them which are asleep* and says *the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first* (1 Thessalonians 4:13,16). Daniel saw the awakening from the dust, some to life and some to contempt; Paul names the first of it — the dead in Messiah (Christ), the righteous seed, who rise first at his coming, that they sorrow not as others which have no hope. The rest of the sleepers wait for the great resurrection, the judgment of the dead.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=4 AND sv.verse_number=16
   AND tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='daniel' AND tv.chapter_number=12 AND tv.verse_number=2
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*Therefore prophesy and say unto them, Thus saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD); Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves, and bring you into the land of Yashar''el (Israel).* (Ezekiel 37:12). To the whole house of Yashar''el (Israel), the dried bones, Yahuah (LORD) promised: *I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves.* This is the resurrection-and-gathering Paul declares: *the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first: Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them* (1 Thessalonians 4:16-17). The opened graves of the two-house people are the dead in Messiah (Christ) who rise first at his coming — the first resurrection, the righteous seed brought up out of Sheol and into the land for the reign. The *Then* of verse 17 waits: the catching-up comes after the reign and the little season. Not a rapture detached from Yashar''el (Israel), but the raising of the house Ezekiel saw.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=4 AND sv.verse_number=16
   AND tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='ezekiel' AND tv.chapter_number=37 AND tv.verse_number=12
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And shall put my spirit in you, and ye shall live, and I shall place you in your own land: then shall ye know that I Yahuah (LORD) have spoken it, and performed it, saith Yahuah (LORD).* (Ezekiel 37:14). Yahuah (LORD) seals the vision of the opened graves: *I will put my spirit in you, and ye shall live, and I shall place you in your own land.* Paul says the raised and the living *shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet Yahuah (Lord) in the air: and so shall we ever be with Yahuah (Lord)* (1 Thessalonians 4:17). Ezekiel''s placing in the land is the reign, when the raised house dwells in its own land; Paul''s *so shall we ever be with Yahuah (Lord)* comes after it — the catching-up after the reign and the little season, the *Come up hither* of Revelation 11:12. The same Spirit-given life runs through both: the house that lives by his Spirit in the land is the people that is ever with him at the end.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=4 AND sv.verse_number=17
   AND tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='ezekiel' AND tv.chapter_number=37 AND tv.verse_number=14
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*In a moment, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trump: for the trumpet shall sound, and the dead shall be raised incorruptible, and we shall be changed.* (1 Corinthians 15:52). Paul names the same trumpet to the Corinthians: *at the last trump... the dead shall be raised incorruptible, and we shall be changed.* Set it beside *the trump of Elohim (God): and the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first* (1 Thessalonians 4:16). The trump of Elohim (God) sounds at his coming, while the Day''s wrath falls, and the righteous seed rise first; the last trump is the seventh trumpet at the end, after the reign and the little season, when the dead are raised and the living are changed and caught up (1 Thessalonians 4:17). Two soundings, two risings, the reign between them — each in its own season.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=4 AND sv.verse_number=16
   AND tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='1-corinthians' AND tv.chapter_number=15 AND tv.verse_number=52
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.* (Matthew 24:31). Yahusha (Jesus) foretold the gathering at the trumpet: *a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds.* Paul too writes of a gathering upward: *we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet Yahuah (Lord) in the air* (1 Thessalonians 4:17). These are not one event. The Olivet trumpet gathers the elect from the four winds at his return — the scattered seed brought home for the reign. The catching-up Paul names at verse 17 comes after the reign and the little season, the *Come up hither* of Revelation 11:12. Both are trumpets of the same King, sounding at the two edges of the reign.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=4 AND sv.verse_number=17
   AND tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='matthew' AND tv.chapter_number=24 AND tv.verse_number=31
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And the earth shall restore those that are asleep in her, and so shall the dust those that dwell in silence, and the secret places shall deliver those souls that were committed to them.* (2 Esdras 7:32). The restored library held the same hope of resurrection: *the earth shall restore those that are asleep in her... and the secret places shall deliver those souls.* This is the rising Paul declares — *them which are asleep... the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first* (1 Thessalonians 4:13,16). The earth restoring the asleep is the hope of resurrection; the dead in Messiah (Christ) are the first of it, the righteous seed raised out of Sheol at his coming. The day the earth gives back all her dead before the seat of judgment is the great resurrection after the reign — two risings, the reign between.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=4 AND sv.verse_number=16
   AND tv.edition_slug='apocrypha' AND tv.book_slug='2-esdras' AND tv.chapter_number=7 AND tv.verse_number=32
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_references x SET note = E'*And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes. For in those days the Elect One shall arise,* (1 Enoch 51:1). The library beholds the day of resurrection: *the earth shall give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received,* and *the Elect One shall arise.* This is the day Paul names — *Yahuah (Lord) himself shall descend from heaven with a shout... and the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first* (1 Thessalonians 4:16). Sheol giving back what it received at the arising of the Elect One is the hope behind the rising of the dead in Messiah (Christ) — the righteous seed brought up out of Sheol at the descending of the King, the first resurrection, that the chosen should be saved.'
  FROM _s434_lu sv, _s434_lu tv
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='1-thessalonians' AND sv.chapter_number=4 AND sv.verse_number=16
   AND tv.edition_slug='enoch' AND tv.book_slug='1-enoch' AND tv.chapter_number=51 AND tv.verse_number=1
   AND x.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND x.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND x.source='manual';

UPDATE cross_reference_threads SET title = E'The coming of our Lord with all his saints (Zechariah 14, Deuteronomy 33)', summary_md = E'Paul closes the chapter with a prayer that the Father may *stablish your hearts unblameable in holiness before Elohim (God), even our Father, at the coming of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) with all his saints* (1 Thessalonians 3:13). The phrase *with all his saints* is not a new revelation but a word the whole library already carried. Zechariah named the day: *Yahuah Elohai (the LORD my God) shall come, and all the saints with thee* (Zechariah 14:5) — the day Yahuah (LORD) stands on the mount of Olives and becomes *king over all the earth.* Moses sang of it at the first: *Yahuah (LORD) came from Sinai... and he came with ten thousands of saints: from his right hand went a fiery law for them* (Deuteronomy 33:2) — the same Yahuah (LORD) surrounded by his holy ones, the same covenant of holiness in which the hearts are now stablished. And the Hebrew library held it as prophecy: *behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His set-apart ones To execute judgement upon all* (1 Enoch 1:9) — the very word Jude quotes by name, *And Enoch also, the seventh from Adam, prophesied of these, saying, Behold, Yahuah (Lord) cometh with ten thousands of his saints* (Jude 14). One coming, one host of holy ones, one day witnessed across Zechariah, Moses, Enoch, and Jude. This is the returning King gathering the one people, the Formed who comes with the saints to judge the ungodly and to receive his own — not a secret rapture severed from Yashar''el (Israel), and not a church that replaced her, but the day of Yahuah the prophets foretold, for which the Father stablishes his people unblameable in holiness. The Father is the One who stablishes; the Son is the One who comes; the saints are the seed of promise he raises up and gathers to himself, for no one descends from heaven with him.'
 WHERE slug='1-thessalonians-3-the-coming-of-our-lord-with-all-his-saints-zechariah-14-deuteronomy-33';

UPDATE cross_reference_threads SET title = E'The dead in Messiah rise first: the trump of the gathering (Isaiah 27, Daniel 12, Ezekiel 37)', summary_md = E'This is the apostle''s great word of the resurrection and the gathering: *I would not have you to be ignorant, brethren, concerning them which are asleep, that ye sorrow not, even as others which have no hope... Yahuah (Lord) himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of Elohim (God): and the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first: Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet Yahuah (Lord) in the air: and so shall we ever be with Yahuah (Lord)* (1 Thessalonians 4:13,16-17). Read it through the whole library, and mark the *Then* (epeita) that opens verse 17: two events, with the whole reign between them — not a secret, pre-tribulation rapture severed from Yashar''el (Israel), and not a separate program for a church that replaced Israel. Verse 16 is his coming while the Day''s wrath falls: the dead in Messiah (Christ), the righteous seed, rise first out of Sheol, and the remnant is kept from the wrath and saved out of it. Verse 17 is the catching-up after the reign and the little season. The *trump of Elohim (God)* is the trumpet of Isaiah: *the great trumpet shall be blown, and they shall come which were ready to perish... and the outcasts... and shall worship Yahuah (LORD) in the holy mount at Jerusalem* (Isaiah 27:13) — the regathering of the scattered outcasts of Yashar''el (Israel). The rising of *the dead in Messiah (Christ)* is the resurrection of the Tanakh: *many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake* (Daniel 12:2); *Thy dead men shall live... Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust... and the earth shall cast out the dead* (Isaiah 26:19); and the opened graves of the whole house of Yashar''el (Israel) — *I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves, and bring you into the land of Yashar''el (Israel)* (Ezekiel 37:12), *I will put my spirit in you, and ye shall live, and I shall place you in your own land* (Ezekiel 37:14). The opened-grave people are brought up and placed in their own land for the reign. The *caught up together... to meet Yahuah (Lord) in the air* comes after it, when the reign and the little season are finished — *so shall we ever be with Yahuah (Lord).* The New Testament sets two more trumpets beside it: *at the last trump: for the trumpet shall sound, and the dead shall be raised incorruptible, and we shall be changed* (1 Corinthians 15:52), and *a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other* (Matthew 24:31). The Olivet trumpet gathers the scattered elect home at his return; the last trump sounds at the end, the seventh trumpet, when the dead are raised and the living changed and caught up. Two events, two risings, the reign between: the righteous seed raised first at his coming, and the catching-up at the end, when the reign and the little season are done. *Wherefore comfort one another with these words* (1 Thessalonians 4:18).'
 WHERE slug='1-thessalonians-4-the-dead-in-messiah-rise-the-trump-of-gathering-isaiah-27-daniel-12';

UPDATE cross_reference_threads SET title = E'The earth gives back her dead: the day of resurrection in the Hebrew library (2 Esdras 7, 1 Enoch 51)', summary_md = E'The hope Paul preached — *the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first* (1 Thessalonians 4:16) — the restored library held before him, beholding the earth and the grave surrendering the asleep. The seer of Esdras saw it: *the earth shall restore those that are asleep in her, and so shall the dust those that dwell in silence, and the secret places shall deliver those souls that were committed to them* (2 Esdras 7:32). And Enoch beheld the same: *in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes. For in those days the Elect One shall arise* (1 Enoch 51:1). The earth restoring the asleep, Sheol giving back what it received at the arising of the Elect One — this is *Yahuah (Lord) himself shall descend from heaven... and the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first.* The hope is one; the risings are two. At his coming the dead in Messiah (Christ) rise first — the righteous seed out of Sheol, the first resurrection, that the chosen should be saved. After the reign the earth gives up the rest of her dead to the judgment of the dead, the great resurrection. Not a secret snatching severed from the people, but the asleep raised each in their own order.'
 WHERE slug='1-thessalonians-4-the-earth-gives-back-her-dead-the-day-of-resurrection-2-esdras-7-1-enoch-51';

